{
 "id": "bigville_decision_core",
 "version": "1.1.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "BIGVILLE DECISION CORE (block 279000) -- the conduct decision is ONE COLLAPSE applied to conduct (the same collapse the eye and the sd loop run), with RESIDUAL as the depth-driver. The four 'parts' are the FACES of one collapse: (0) the SHALLOW collapse = a genuinely compiled/cached net (native NetForward over a NetworkAssemblage) settling in one pass over an availability-filtered consideration set -- the connectionist-descent face; the RESIDUAL (surprise = |cached value - grounded model value|) IS the arbiter -- a collapse with residual above settle_tol has NOT settled, so it CONTINUES; (N) the DEEPER collapse = a model-based symbolic Argmax that runs ONLY because the shallow pass left residual (the symbolic-rewrite face; carries rationalise_gain so deliberation can rationalise, not only override -- correction #2); (settle-back) INTERNALIZATION = net_collapse writing the settled result into the held net (the SAME collapse at a slower timescale, Mattar&Daw MB->MF replay), so the shallow pass settles it directly next time = the automation curve. 'yes...wait...no' is ONE collapse trace: fast settle (yes) -> residual (wait, not settled) -> deeper settle (no). Two coupled knobs (correction #1): depth (order) x precision (settle_tol, the collapse tolerance) -- residual, not a bolted-on threshold, drives it; scalar residual logged, no depletion term. Violence sits on BOTH the shallow and deep faces. Every face is a rule composing existing DSL Terms + the native net collapse ops (NetForward / net_collapse); ZERO new Rust. OFF by default (self_load_only). Falsifiers: replay_gain<=0 freezes the settle-back (flat curve); deepen_enabled=0 caps depth at the shallow collapse (pure order-0).",
 "nodes": [],
 "edges": [],
 "productions": [],
 "concepts": [],
