  {
   "name": "dc_collapse_settle",
   "batch": false,
   "comment": "SETTLED SHALLOW. The residual IS the arbiter -- there is no separate 'should I escalate?' decision. A collapse whose residual is within settle_tol HAS settled; it commits the held candidate directly (order-0, deepened=0). Also settles here when depth is capped (deepen_enabled=0 = the collapse cannot go deeper) -- pure order-0 / habitual. No write-back needed: a settled shallow state is one the held net already predicts. This is the impulsive/automatic path.",
